#### 9. Add Tracking Information
**PUT** `/server/fulfillment/add-tracking/:id`

Add or update tracking information. Can be done before or after fulfilling.

**Request Body:**
```json
{
  "tracking": "1Z999AA10123456784", // Required
  "tracking_link": "https://ups.com/track/...", // Optional
  "carrier_name": "UPS" // Optional
}
```

**What it does:**
- Updates tracking, tracking_link, carrier_name
- If status is FULFILLED and delivery_status is PREPARED, changes to LABEL_CREATED
- Does NOT change status if UNFULFILLED
- Does NOT deduct inventory
- Creates tracking history if delivery_status changed

**Example:**
```bash
curl -X PUT "http://localhost:3010/api/server/fulfillment/add-tracking/fulfillment-uuid" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "tracking": "1Z999AA10123456784",
    "tracking_link": "https://ups.com/track/...",
    "carrier_name": "UPS"
  }'
```

**Flexible workflow:**
- Can add tracking before fulfilling (plan ahead)
- Can add tracking after fulfilling (label created later)
- Can update tracking if wrong number entered

---

#### 10. Update Status
**PUT** `/server/fulfillment/update-status/:id`

Update delivery status and/or carrier status as package moves through delivery journey.

**Request Body:**
```json
{
  "delivery_status": "IN_TRANSIT", // Optional
  "carrier_status": "Package at sorting facility - Praha 5", // Optional
  "notes": "Carrier scan at 14:30" // Optional
}
```

**At least one of `delivery_status` or `carrier_status` must be provided.**

**Delivery Status Values:**
- PENDING, PREPARED, LABEL_CREATED, IN_TRANSIT, OUT_FOR_DELIVERY, DELIVERED, FAILED, RETURNED

**What it does:**
- Updates delivery_status (if provided)
- Updates carrier_status (if provided)
- Creates tracking history
- Does NOT change fulfillment status
- Does NOT touch inventory

**Examples:**

Update delivery status only:
```bash
curl -X PUT "http://localhost:3010/api/server/fulfillment/update-status/fulfillment-uuid" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"delivery_status": "IN_TRANSIT"}'
```

Update carrier status only:
```bash
curl -X PUT "http://localhost:3010/api/server/fulfillment/update-status/fulfillment-uuid" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"carrier_status": "Package picked up from warehouse"}'
```

Update both:
```bash
curl -X PUT "http://localhost:3010/api/server/fulfillment/update-status/fulfillment-uuid" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "delivery_status": "OUT_FOR_DELIVERY",
    "carrier_status": "On delivery vehicle - driver Jan Novák"
  }'
```

**Use cases:**
- Manual status updates from dashboard
- Carrier webhook notifications
- API integration with shipping providers
- Customer service updates

