## 🔄 **Inventory & Order Status Flow**

### Complete Inventory Lifecycle

```
ORDER CREATION
├─ Order created
├─ Inventory RESERVED (not deducted)
├─ Backorders created (if insufficient stock)
└─ Order status: ACTIVE (if paid) or HOLD (if backorders)

FULFILLMENT CREATION
├─ Fulfillment created
├─ Items assigned to package
├─ order_item.fulfilled_quantity updated (tracking only)
├─ Inventory: Still RESERVED (no change)
└─ order.fulfillment_status: Still UNFULFILLED (no change)

FULFILLMENT FULFILLED ← Inventory deducted here!
├─ Status: UNFULFILLED → FULFILLED
├─ Delivery status: PENDING → PREPARED
├─ Inventory DEDUCTED (reservations fulfilled)
├─ Physical stock removed
└─ order.fulfillment_status: Changes to PARTIALLY_FULFILLED or FULFILLED

TRACKING ADDED
├─ Tracking info saved
├─ Delivery status: PREPARED → LABEL_CREATED
├─ Inventory: No change (already deducted)
└─ order.fulfillment_status: No change

PACKAGE SHIPS
├─ Delivery status: → IN_TRANSIT
├─ Carrier updates via webhooks
└─ Inventory: No change

PACKAGE DELIVERED
├─ Delivery status: → DELIVERED
└─ Order complete
```

### Key Decision Points

**When creating fulfillment:**
- ✅ Assigns items to package
- ❌ Does NOT deduct inventory
- ❌ Does NOT change order.fulfillment_status

**When fulfilling:**
- ✅ Deducts inventory
- ✅ Changes order.fulfillment_status
- ✅ This is the point of commitment

**When adding tracking:**
- ✅ Updates tracking info
- ❌ Does NOT deduct inventory
- ❌ Does NOT change order.fulfillment_status

### Order Fulfillment Status Calculation

The system calculates `order.fulfillment_status` by checking quantities in **FULFILLED fulfillments only**:

```
Total order quantity: 10 items

Fulfillment #1: UNFULFILLED, 3 items
Fulfillment #2: FULFILLED, 5 items
Fulfillment #3: UNFULFILLED, 2 items

Calculation:
- Total in FULFILLED fulfillments: 5 items
- 5 < 10 → order.fulfillment_status: PARTIALLY_FULFILLED

After fulfilling #1:
- Total in FULFILLED fulfillments: 8 items (5 + 3)
- 8 < 10 → order.fulfillment_status: PARTIALLY_FULFILLED

After fulfilling #3:
- Total in FULFILLED fulfillments: 10 items (5 + 3 + 2)
- 10 = 10 → order.fulfillment_status: FULFILLED
```

