## 📋 **Best Practices**

### Fulfillment Lifecycle
1. **Create fulfillments early** - Plan packaging without committing inventory
2. **Fulfill when ready** - Only call FULFILL when package is actually packed
3. **Track status changes** - Order status updates when fulfillments are FULFILLED
4. **Use UNFULFILL for mistakes** - Before shipping, use UNFULFILL to reverse
5. **Use RETURNS after shipping** - Once IN_TRANSIT, use returns system

### Inventory Management
6. **Inventory deducts on FULFILL** - Not on CREATE, not on ADD-TRACKING
7. **Monitor UNFULFILLED** - These are packages waiting to be prepared
8. **CANCEL safely** - Only UNFULFILLED can be cancelled (no inventory impact)
9. **UNFULFILL carefully** - Reverses inventory, use before carrier pickup

### Tracking & Status
10. **Tracking is optional** - Can fulfill without tracking (store pickup, etc.)
11. **Add tracking anytime** - Before or after fulfilling
12. **Update status regularly** - Use UPDATE-STATUS for delivery progress
13. **Carrier webhooks** - Integrate for automatic status updates

### Multi-Package Orders
14. **Use partial fulfillments** - Split orders into multiple packages
15. **Fulfill independently** - Each package has its own lifecycle
16. **Order status auto-calculates** - Based on FULFILLED fulfillments

### Error Handling
17. **RESHIP for lost packages** - Don't try to unfulfill shipped packages
18. **Check inventory before reship** - RESHIP validates stock availability
19. **Keep tracking history** - Every status change is logged automatically

